## Done when

- [ ] `html` takes no tap highlight at any pointer.
- [ ] Under `(pointer: coarse)`, `html` takes `user-select: none` and `-webkit-touch-callout: none`, and fields take `user-select: text`.
- [ ] `.chat-panel` restores all three.
- [ ] `board.css` sets no tap highlight, and the #2015 zone rules are gone.
- [ ] The 2FA key's `-webkit-user-select: all` is in.
- [ ] `highlight.test.ts` is green, including the stylesheet lint tests (`palette`, `typescale`, `surfaces`, `motion`, `cursors`, `typography`).
- [ ] The full `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, typecheck and eslint on the touched test files are green.
- [ ] The harness's checks pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `catalog check`, `patches check`, `spec check`, clippy, cargo tests and the `wire` cleanliness test.
- [ ] The phone check ran, or the final message says it did not.
- [ ] README paragraph added.

## Risks

- `cursors.test.ts` slices `index.css` between `@media (pointer: fine)` and the first `html {`, and requires the exact `html {\n  cursor: var(--cursor-glove, auto);\n}`. Keep both untouched and put the new rules after l.446.
- `user-select: none` on `html` is inherited by everything. Anything that must stay selectable declares its own value: fields and `.chat-panel` (steps 1–2), and the 2FA key (step 4). Any other copyable text on a phone becomes unselectable, as the issue asks.
- Removing the #2015 zone rule means a legal zone no longer greys on a tap either. That is intended; its `data-legal` glow remains its feedback. The two remaining #2015 behavior tests (disabled group fires nothing) are unaffected.
- `(pointer: coarse)` is false on a desktop, so e2e and the pixel specs (fine pointer) see only the invisible tap-colour rule.
- Do not add an `#[allow]`, an `eslint-disable` or a skipped test. `highlight.test.ts` carries no `R<n>` id.

## Open questions

- **Decision, for a person to veto:** the 2FA key keeps being selectable on a phone (step 4). It is a deliberate exception to "nothing but the chat". The alternative is to leave `two-step.css` alone and let iPhones lose the key's copy path, or to add a copy button. A copy button is out of scope here.
- Acceptance item 3 (a long press at 390x844 with touch) is proven only by the CSS unit test and the best-effort walkthrough in step 8, not by CI. No Cypress spec can emulate a coarse pointer here.
- Difficulty `medium` holds: web CSS, one test, one README paragraph, about 7 files, with no engine, AI, migration or cross-crate change.
